.TH AENIGMA-UPDATE 8 "2026-08-13" "aenigma-tools 1.0.0" "Aenigma Administration Tools"
.SH NAME
aenigma-update \- refresh the package index and install the latest
available Aenigma package
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B aenigma-update
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B aenigma-update
refreshes the local package index and installs the latest available
version of the
.B aenigma
package via
.BR apt-get (8).
It takes no options or arguments.
.PP
The script performs the following actions:
.IP \(bu 2
Runs
.B "apt-get update"
to refresh the package index.
.IP \(bu 2
Runs
.B "apt-get install aenigma"
non-interactively to install
.B aenigma
if not already present, or upgrade it to the latest version
available from the currently configured package sources.
.PP
.B aenigma-update
performs no version comparison and takes no action on the
.B aenigma
service itself; whether and how the service is restarted after an
upgrade is left entirely to the
.B aenigma
package's own maintainer scripts.
.PP
.B aenigma-update
is shipped as part of the main
.B aenigma
package. It is intended to be invoked periodically by the
.B aenigma-update.timer
/
.B aenigma-update.service
unit pair, which are packaged separately in the optional
.B aenigma-auto-update
package; installing
.B aenigma
alone does not enable automatic updates.
.PP
.B aenigma-update
must be run as root.
.SH OPTIONS
.B aenigma-update
takes no command-line options.
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
The package index was refreshed and
.B "apt-get install aenigma"
completed successfully, whether or not a new version was actually
installed.
.TP
.B 1
The script was not run as root, or either
.B apt-get
invocation failed.
.SH EXAMPLES
Check for and apply the latest available
.B aenigma
package:
.PP
.RS
.EX
sudo aenigma-update
.EE
.RE
.SH NOTES
Any restart of the
.B aenigma
service following an installed upgrade is handled by the
.B aenigma
package's own
.B postinst
maintainer script (via
.BR dh_installsystemd (1)'s
default upgrade behavior), not by
.BR aenigma-update
itself. This script only ensures the package is present and
up to date; it does not verify that the service is running, or
report whether a version change actually occurred.
.PP
This script does not pin, hold back, or otherwise limit which
version of
.B aenigma
.B apt-get
considers the latest available; it always installs whatever version
is newest according to the currently configured package sources at
the time it runs.
.PP
For scheduled, unattended execution, see the
.B aenigma-auto-update
package, which installs a systemd timer running this script daily.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR apt-get (8),
.BR aenigma-start (8)
.SH AUTHOR
Romulus-Emanuel Ruja <romulus.ruja@aenigma.ro>
